ides which invoices show as overdue.","options":["One configurable payment term in days for all customers","Payment terms set per customer"],"reason":"Needs no new customer field, and per-customer terms weren't asked for.","recommended":"One configurable payment term in days for all customers","score":9,"spans":["59-invoice-lifecycle"],"text":"How is the invoice due date calculated: the same payment terms for every customer, or terms set per customer?","topic":"payments","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","difference":"D-5.62","id":"Q-9","impact":3,"impactReason":"Invoice creation is a write of financial data.","options":["In the same save: if the invoice can't be created, the Delivered status isn't saved either","Created by a background process shortly after the status is saved","Same save for the invoice record; the PDF is made afterwards"],"reason":"The §72 acceptance criterion needs the invoice to exist as soon as Delivered is saved, and keeping PDF problems separate means they can't block delivery.","recommended":"Same save for the invoice record; the PDF is made afterwards","score":9,"spans":["62-background-jobs","59-invoice-lifecycle","72-acceptance-criteria","64-pdf-generation"],"text":"Is the invoice created in the same save as the 'Delivered' status change, or later by a background process?","uncertainty":3},{"category":"data-model","id":"Q-10","impact":3,"impactReason":"Financial record.","options":["Paid status, payment date and the staff member who marked it","Also payment method and amount (allowing part-payments)","Status only"],"reason":"Enough for the mark-paid rule and the audit trail, with no part-payment logic.","recommended":"Paid status, payment date and the staff member who marked it","score":9,"spans":["59-invoice-lifecycle","67-business-rules-summary"],"text":"What is recorded when staff mark an invoice paid?","topic":"payments","uncertainty":3},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-11","impact":3,"impactReason":"Affects money handling and changes to order data.","options":["Neither: payment status is tracked manually and orders can't be amended","Staff can amend orders before dispatch; no online payments","Both order amendments and online payment taking are in scope"],"reason":"The final scope summary is the authoritative list for the first release.","recommended":"Neither: payment status is tracked manually and orders can't be amended","score":6,"spans":["76-invoicing-payments","76-order-lifecycle"],"text":"'Order amendments' and 'Payments' appear in the backend checklist, but the scope summary lists only 'Payment status' and no amendments. Are they in the first release?","uncertainty":2},{"category":"scope","id":"Q-12","impact":3,"impactReason":"Decides which data is written and who can see it.","options":["Changes to orders, prices, products and users (who, when, what); admin-only view","Same, viewable by staff and admin","Also log sign-ins and exports"],"reason":"This covers the key business changes without logging everything.","recommended":"Changes to orders, prices, products and users (who, when, what); admin-only view","score":6,"spans":["76-audit-history"],"text":"What does the audit history record, and who can view it?","topic":"audit","uncertainty":2},{"category":"roles","id":"Q-13","impact":3,"impactReason":"Defines permissions throughout the system.","options":["Customer user, Staff, Admin","Customer user and Customer admin (manages own company's users), Staff, Admin","Also a customer approver role for order sign-off"],"reason":"These are the three roles the scope implies.","recommended":"Customer user, Staff, Admin","score":6,"spans":["76-customer-auth-and-access","76-administration"],"text":"Which user roles are there?","topic":"roles","uncertainty":2},{"category":"roles","id":"Q-14","impact":3,"impactReason":"Decides who sees which orders and invoices.","options":["Yes, all data is shared at company level","Each user sees only their own orders and templates; invoices are company-wide","Co