79","risk":"low","text":"Which browsers are supported? → assumed: The latest two versions of Chrome, Edge, Safari and Firefox."},{"fromDefault":"volumes","fromQuestion":"Q26","fromSpan":["75-technology-stack"],"id":"ASM-80","risk":"low","text":"What scale is expected (customers, users, products, orders per day)? → assumed: Up to 1,000 users and 100,000 records in the first year."},{"fromDefault":"hosting","fromQuestion":"Q27","fromSpan":["75-technology-stack"],"id":"ASM-81","risk":"low","text":"Where is it hosted? → assumed: One cloud region, in the client's cloud account."},{"fromDefault":"accessibility","fromQuestion":"Q28","fromSpan":["76-responsive-mobile-experience"],"id":"ASM-82","risk":"low","text":"What accessibility level is required? → assumed: WCAG 2.1 AA on the main flows."},{"fromQuestion":"Q29","fromSpan":["76-customer-company-management","76-basket-checkout-delivery-scheduling"],"id":"ASM-83","risk":"low","text":"What does 'Account/address management' cover for customers? → assumed: Addresses are managed by staff only; customers pick from them at checkout"}],"conflicts":["Section 3.1 lets a Buyer 'View their company's orders' and 'View invoices', but section 3.2 lists 'View orders placed by other users within the same customer company' and 'View company invoices' as extras for the Account Manager. These can't both hold, so it is unclear whether Buyers see only their own orders or the whole company's.","D-1.1: one reading lets customers see an invoice only after the order is Delivered (when it is created); the other two place no restriction on order status.","I-3 promises 'current stock availability', but section 9 says stock comes only from a nightly CSV, so it can be up to a day old.","Saved basket templates (section 16) are listed as a Buyer capability but are missing from the intent list (I-13, I-15).","§62 lists 'Invoice generation' as background processing, but the §72 acceptance criterion says the invoice is created as soon as the Delivered status is saved (D-5.62).","§58 shows 'Invoice Created' as a step in the order lifecycle after Delivered, while §59 treats invoice creation as the start of a separate invoice lifecycle.","§59 draws Unpaid, Paid and Overdue as parallel branches from Invoice Created, not as an order of transitions (Unpaid → Paid/Overdue, Overdue → Paid).","Rule 10 lets staff edit orders only before confirmation, yet §43 requires an 'Order amendment' email, which suggests amendments may also happen after confirmation.","§46 says deleting a user keeps their records, while rule 15 talks about 'deactivation'. It's unclear whether users are ever actually deleted.","Section 76 says the estimate depends on an 'Open Questions' section, but that section isn't in the request.","The backend checklist includes 'Order amendments' and 'Payments', but the final scope summary lists only 'Payment status' and no order amendments.","The integrations checklist includes 'Hosting/deployment', which isn't an integration; it overlaps with the DevOps section."],"differences":[{"id":"D-1.1","readings":[{"behaviour":5,"sketch":3,"summary":"Invoice is only viewable once order reaches Delivered status (since invoice is created at that point)"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Customer views list of invoices and opens invoice detail with payment status without restriction on order status"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":2,"summary":"Customer can view a list of invoices with payment status (paid/unpaid/overdue) without restriction on order status"}],"span":"I-5","topic":"Invoice viewing availability"},{"id":"D-1.52","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Invalid login shows a clear 'incorrect credentials' style message"},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":3,"summary":"Invalid login shows a generic 'invalid credentials' message without revealing whether username or password was wrong"}],"span":"52-error-handling","topic":"Invalid login message specificity"},{"id":"D-2.54","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Loading indicators shown during async operations (catalogue, search, etc.)"},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"During order submission or checkout, submit control is disabled/hidden to prevent duplicate submissions while loading"}],"span":"54-loading-states","topic":"Duplicate submission prevention during loading"},{"id":"D-3.56","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":2,"summary":"Staff can navigate to and use staff sign in as first screen in list of 11 staff screens"},{"behaviour":1,"sketch":3,"summary":"Staff sign-in is a separate login flow/route from customer sign-in"}],"span":"56-main-staff-screens","topic":"Staff sign-in flow separation from customer"},{"id":"D-4.59","readings":[{"behaviour":3,"sketch":1,"summary":"Invoice may transition to Overdue status automatically based on rules to be defined"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"A scheduled job transitions Unpaid invoices past their due date to Overdue status automatically"}],"span":"59-invoice-lifecycle","topic":"Automatic vs manual transition to Overdue status"},{"id":"D-5.62","readings":[{"behaviour":2,"sketch":1,"summary":"Invoice generation runs automatically upon order delivery as a background process"},{"behaviour":2,"sketch":3,"summary":"Invoice generation is triggered synchronously on the Delivered status change"}],"span":"62-background-jobs","topic":"Invoice generation timing: async background process vs synchronous on status change"},{"id":"D-6.64","readings":[{"behaviour":0,"sketch":1,"summary":"Portal generates an invoice PDF and makes it downloadable"},{"behaviour":0,"sketch":3,"summary":"PDF is generated once per invoice on creation and reused for subsequent downloads rather than regenerated each time"}],"span":"64-pdf-generation","topic":"PDF generation timing: once on creation and reused vs potentially on each download"}],"round":1}